# CMMC L1 / NIST 800-171 3.14.4 - Update malicious code protection mechanisms
# Platform: M365 (Microsoft Secure Score)
# Check type: m365_graph_query against /security/secureScores

META
    esp_id `cmmc-l1-3-14-4-m365-av-updates-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `m365`
    criticality `medium`

    title `CMMC L1 SI.L1-3.14.4: Update malicious code protection mechanisms`
    description `Validates that a Microsoft Secure Score reading exists for the tenant. Secure Score continuously evaluates the freshness and configuration of malicious-code-protection components and is the tenant-wide measurement of update posture for those mechanisms.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `m365,cmmc-l1,nist-800-171,3-14-4,si,av-updates,secure-score`

    control_mapping `NIST-800-171:3.14.4`
    control_objective `3.14.4`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `M365:tenant:security-posture`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Ensure the tenant is generating a Secure Score reading and that the SPN has SecurityEvents.Read.All scope to retrieve it. Review the Secure Score control evaluations periodically for malicious-code-protection items below threshold and remediate.`

    component_id `comp-m365-security-posture`

    impl_3_14_4 `Malicious-code-protection mechanisms are kept current through centrally managed signature and engine updates delivered by the antimalware vendor and tracked tenant-wide via the security posture measurement system. The security posture reading exposes per-control evaluations including signature freshness, real-time-protection enablement, and engine version currency; declining scores on these items trigger administrative review and corrective action. The measurement runs continuously rather than at fixed intervals, ensuring lapses in update delivery surface promptly.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT secure_score
        path `security/secureScores`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE secure_score_present
        found boolean = true
        record
            field rows.*.currentScore int >= 0 at_least_one
            field rows.*.maxScore int > 0 at_least_one
        record_end
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN m365_graph_query
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF secure_score_present
            OBJECT_REF secure_score
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
